<title>SPAIN: Mapfre unit buys Venezuelan insurance firm.</title>
<headline>Mapfre unit buys Venezuelan insurance firm.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mapfre Internacional, a unit of Spain's Corporacion Mapfre, has bought Venezuela's largest insurance company Seguros la Seguridad, a statement from Mapfre said on Friday.</p>
<p>Mapfre will pay around 3.5 billion to 3.8 billion pesetas for the insurer, according to current company estimates.</p>
<p>Seguros la Seguridad has a 20 percent market share in Venezuela, with premium revenue of around 60 billion bolivars (16.3 billion pesetas).</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
